sequenceDiagram
    participant EH as EvalHub
    participant AD as Adapter pod<br/>python main.py
    participant HF as Hugging Face Hub<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant MS as Model endpoint<br/>/v1/completions
    participant ML as MLflow
    participant REG as OCI registry<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant OP as LMEval controller<br/>(trustyai-service-operator)
    participant JP as Job pod<br/>python -m lm_eval
    participant S3 as S3-compatible storage

    Note over EH,REG: Flow 1: EvalHub adapter evaluation job
    EH->>AD: Mount /meta/job.json and /test_data<br/>(file mount, Kubernetes)
    AD->>AD: Validate job spec path under /meta<br/>Enable HF offline mode if /test_data staged
    opt Online mode (no staged data)
        AD->>HF: GET datasets / tokenizer<br/>HTTPS TLS, HF_TOKEN optional
        HF-->>AD: Assets
    end
    AD->>EH: report_status (phases)<br/>HTTP/HTTPS, eval-hub-sdk auth
    loop Evaluation requests (num_concurrent at most 128)
        AD->>MS: POST /v1/completions<br/>HTTP/HTTPS (TLS if https), Bearer OPENAI_API_KEY
        MS-->>AD: Completions
    end
    AD->>ML: Save results (callbacks.mlflow.save)<br/>HTTP/HTTPS TLS
    opt exports.oci set
        AD->>REG: Push results OCI artifact<br/>HTTPS TLS, registry creds
    end
    AD->>EH: report_results (final)<br/>errors sanitized of secrets

    Note over OP,S3: Flow 2: TrustyAI LMEvalJob CLI run
    OP->>JP: Launch pod: python -m lm_eval ...
    opt S3 download
        JP->>S3: GET models/datasets<br/>HTTPS TLS, AWS keys
        S3-->>JP: Objects into hf_home
    end
    JP->>HF: Datasets/tokenizers (or local hf_home, my_catalogs)<br/>HTTPS 443, HF_TOKEN optional
    HF-->>JP: Assets
    JP->>MS: Requests to model endpoint or in-process model<br/>HTTP/HTTPS, API key
    MS-->>JP: Responses
    JP->>JP: Write results to /opt/app-root/src/output
